# Build-context filter for `docker build -f Dockerfile.server`.
#
# Without this file, `docker build` uploads the entire repo to the (remote)
# builder. A dev machine's `target/` dir alone can be 50+ GB of cargo debug
# artifacts; the resulting upload tail on `flyctl deploy` is measured in tens
# of minutes. With this filter the build context drops to a few MB — the
# Rust source under crates/, the workspace Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock, the
# rust-toolchain.toml, and not much else.
#
# Anything `cargo build --release --bin midnight-manual-server` does not
# consume can be excluded. The Dockerfile bakes `crates/mnm-store/migrations`
# into the runtime stage explicitly, so don't exclude that subtree.

# Cargo build artifacts — by far the biggest contributor on a dev machine.
target/

# VCS internals and CI definitions.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.gitmodules
.github/

# Editor / IDE / OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Local agent / workflow state — never consumed by the build.
.claude/
.midnight-expert/
.sdd/

# Top-level operator-only docs.
CONSTITUTION.md
CLAUDE.md

# Documentation, spec, and discovery artifacts — not consumed by `cargo build`.
docs/
specs/
discovery/
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
SECURITY.md
LICENSE
NOTICE

# Test fixtures and benches — not compiled into the release binary.
corpus/
benches/
tests/

# Dev / deploy config not consumed by the Rust build inside the image.
fly.toml
justfile
Justfile
.envrc
.nvmrc

# Don't include Dockerfiles or the dockerignore itself in the context.
.dockerignore
Dockerfile*

# Scratch / backup files.
*.bak
*.backup
